🟢 8. CACHING
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Repeated request
      ↓
Do we really need DB every time?

Cache:

Request
  ↓
Cache
 ├── HIT  → Return
 └── MISS
       ↓
     Database
       ↓
      Cache
       ↓
     Return

Cache Hit
→ Data found.

Cache Miss
→ Data not found → DB.


HashMap intuition:
→ Works for simple/local caching.

Problems at scale:
→ Limited memory
→ Each server has separate cache
→ Restart loses data
→ Servers don't share cache


Distributed cache:
→ Shared fast cache across servers.
→ Example: Redis.


