🟢 10. LATENCY vs THROUGHPUT
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Latency
→ Time for ONE request.

Throughput
→ Amount of work handled per unit time.

Example:
50 ms latency
1000 requests/sec throughput


Chat:
→ Low latency important.

Batch processing:
→ High throughput often important.

Both may matter.


